#
# Named "returning" because `titlestate.py show --device nova` reports a
# Burnout Revenge profile "found" on this disk (since 2026-09-30T01:36:36Z)
# -- but Load Profile on the SAVE/LOAD prompt answers "There are no profiles
# to load" (shot 003-profile-list.png), the same trap lane.routeprep's pass-1
# evidence showed. So titlestate's record does not mean the profile is
# loadable in-game on this disk; the route below falls through to Create
# Profile every time, same as a true first run would. Until that is
# resolved (nav.py/titlestate.py/saves.py are not this lane's files; see
# dispatch/board-requests/titleroutes.md), this one route covers both
# variants -- there is no working "returning" path to record separately.
#
# Flow, corrected against lane.routeprep's Burnout-3-derived guesses (several
# differ):
#   attract FMV -> title "Press START to continue" (START) -> SAVE/LOAD:
#   "Would you like to create or load a profile?", Load Profile highlighted
#   (A) -> "There are no profiles to load" (A dismisses) -> back to the same
#   prompt, flick DOWN to Create Profile (A) -> an Autosave consent prompt
#   (NOT a name keyboard as guessed), Yes highlighted (A) -> name keyboard,
#   "Burnout_" prefilled, DONE highlighted (A) -> a profile-SLOT picker
#   (NOT a storage/saving notice as guessed), "Profile 1" (empty) highlighted
#   (A) -> main menu, WORLD TOUR highlighted (A) -> rank select, "1" NEW
#   highlighted (A) -> location select, Sunshine Keys highlighted (A) ->
#   event-type select, a NEW event icon highlighted (A) -> car select,
#   default car (A) -> a long loading/tips montage (~100 s, several distinct
#   screens: city skyline thumbnails, grayscale flyover crash reel, the
#   Burnout Revenge logo card) -> an event brief ("TRAFFIC ATTACK: check
#   traffic to beat the Score Targets", gold/silver/bronze cash targets),
#   car already stopped in the world, "Continue" (A) -> gameplay starts
#   immediately with no separate grid/start-light wait: the car is already
#   moving at 70 mph the instant control returns.
#
# Player control confirmed two ways: LX max for 1.1s changed the car's lane
# and road section entirely (021-steer-right.png, a boost-lane shortcut);
# the play pattern below then registered live "TRAFFIC CHECK" / "NEAR MISS"
# scores and raised the money counter from $0 to $14,550
