# Traffic Attack (the event this route lands in) is a short timed event:
# the frames that found this route show it ends well under a minute after
# the mark (docs/lanes/burnoutloop1012/NOTES.md). Once it ends, Burnout
# Revenge holds on a RESULTS screen until a button is pressed -- the drive
# pattern below never pressed one, so a run that reached RESULTS sat
# there, replay moving behind the panel, for the rest of the confirmation.
# `press B` (Retry) below restarts the same event; it is a no-op if the
# race is still running and B does nothing there, so the cadence is
# chosen to bound the alternative: if B turns out to be a live race
# control (e.g. a handbrake), it can only ever land once per 18s of
# driving, never every loop.
#
# RESULTS is not one screen with three prompts -- it is at least two,
# and no frame on disk shows all three together (that claim, in an
# earlier draft of this comment, was never supported by a frame; fixed
# here, lane.burnoutunlock1012, #433):
#   - no medal earned: Retry (B) / More details (Y) only (confirmation 1,
#     `frames/f00016.png`, run `1-1791793410-lane.local-336876`).
#   - a medal earned: More details (Y) / Continue (A) only, **no Retry**
#     (confirmation 2, `frames/f00044.png`, run
#     `1-1791800854-lane.local-2819291`, device time 03:56:35 -- "MEDAL
#     AWARDED BRONZE", "NEW EVENT UNLOCKED!").
# `press B` is a no-op on the medal variant (no Retry to press); the
# `press A` 0.3s later is still Continue there, same as on the no-medal
# brief-dismiss case this pair was built for -- but Continue off a
# medalled RESULTS leaves the event for WORLD TOUR, not back into a race,
# and nothing below this comment can tell those two Continues apart to
# press differently. See docs/lanes/burnoutunlock1012/NOTES.md for the
# full state table, why confirmation 2 got stuck there, and why no fix
# is applied here.
#
# A Retry that lands reaches the next screen within at most 14.3s (measured
# in docs/lanes/burnoutbrief1012/NOTES.md; nothing on disk gives a lower
# bound), past which the loop sat on the event brief for "TRAFFIC ATTACK --
# Check traffic to beat the Score Targets!" with no prompt but Continue (A)
# -- B does nothing there, so a run that reached the brief this way never
# left it. `press A` below, right after `press B`, dismisses that brief.
# The 0.3s gap between the two presses is short on purpose: B must reach
# RESULTS before A can, since A on RESULTS is Continue, which leaves the
# event for screens no route here has recorded. A 0.3s gap leaves only
# ~1.4% of this ~22s loop (0.3 / ~22) exposed to a race ending in that
# exact slice between the two presses, and is still many multiples of the
# 60ms a press is held (perf/pad.sh) -- long enough for the game to see two
# separate inputs, not one. No lower bound on the transition is needed:
# either this iteration's A lands mid-load (a no-op there, same as B would
# be) and the next iteration's A, ~22s later, dismisses the settled brief,
# or the brief is already up by 0.3s and this iteration's A dismisses it
# directly. Either way the brief clears within one loop cycle (~22s), not
# the 12+ minutes it sat for before this fix. If A turns out to be a live
# race control, it is bound by the same cadence already accepted for B: at
# most once per ~22s outer iteration, not every 6s inner-loop tick.
repeat forever {
    repeat 3 {
        axis RT max
        wait 1.5
        axis LX min
        wait 1.5
        axis LX max
        wait 1.5
        axis LX mid
        wait 1.5
    }
    axis RT min
    wait 0.3
    press B
    wait 0.3
    press A
    wait 1.0
}
